In mkroom.c -

struct permonst *
courtmon()
{
        int     i = rn2(60) + rn2(3*level_difficulty());
        if (i > 100)            return(mkclass(S_DRAGON,0));
        else if (i > 95)        return(mkclass(S_GIANT,0));
        else if (i > 85)        return(mkclass(S_TROLL,0));
        else if (i > 75)        return(mkclass(S_CENTAUR,0));
        else if (i > 60)        return(mkclass(S_ORC,0));
        else if (i > 45)        return(&mons[PM_BUGBEAR]);
        else if (i > 30)        return(&mons[PM_HOBGOBLIN]);
        else if (i > 15)        return(mkclass(S_GNOME,0));
        else                    return(mkclass(S_KOBOLD,0));
}

Looking through the code, the other place that a dragon
can be created out-of-depth is by any monster who can
cast the "summon nasties" spell successfully.  Rodney
can, as well as some A, L and &.  None are likely in the
early levels with one notable exception:

A good way to get a dragon in the early game is to do a
same-species sacrafice to summon a demon, then anger the
demon but don't kill it until it has cast the summon
nasties spell enough times to gate in at least one
dragon.  Given the other monsters in the nasties list
and the level characters usually are in the early game,
is may get you a dragon but it will amount certainly
kill you as well.



